{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>חכם, קצר</b> — two words joined. That is, he fears HaShem and turns away from evil, and a fool becomes enraged and angry with others, and trusts that he will live; and one who is short-tempered will become enraged at every act of folly." "<b>ואיש מזמות</b> — evil schemes, he hates. That is, HaShem hates him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Reading קצר as a two-word quotation from the verse (חכם קצר); the comment explains the compressed phrase by pairing it with Psalm 34:14 (fear HaShem, turn from evil) and contrasting the fool's self-confidence."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:46.113902239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}